[brief] Sterile neutrino dark matter is jointly constrained by BBN (via N_eff and primordial Yp and D/H from active-sterile thermalization/oscillations) and by X-ray searches for the radiative decay nu_s -> n
**Survey** — 32 tools on 3 servers, 6 read-only probes, 6 papers found.

Sterile neutrino dark matter is jointly constrained by BBN (via N_eff and primordial Yp and D/H from active-sterile thermalization/oscillations) and by X-ray searches for the radiative decay nu_s -> nu + gamma (E=m_s/2). Standard Dodelson-Widrow production is essentially excluded by the combination of BBN N_eff limits and NuSTAR/Chandra/XMM line limits, while resonant Shi-Fuller production with large lepton asymmetry L~0.1-1 and non-thermal inflaton-decay production during reheating reopen parameter space at small mixing. Recent BBN analyses with precise D/H and He-4 allow L>1 at T>20 MeV to be consistent with BBN, weakening earlier BBN exclusions, and recent NuSTAR M31 (1.2 Ms) and Galactic bulge/plane analyses provide the strongest X-ray limits for 6-40 keV masses. The two weakest prior claims are typically (i) that BBN alone excludes eV-keV mixing above sin^2 2theta ~1e-4 independent of L, and (ii) that X-ray non-detections exclude all DW-motivated DM without accounting for alternative production and field-of-view systematics.

Quantities worth checking: N_eff from sterile thermalization vs Planck+BBN limit; Primordial Yp (He-4 mass fraction) shift vs observed Yp=0.245 +/- 0.003; Primordial D/H vs observed (2.53 +/- 0.04)e-5; Sterile mass m_s and mixing sin^2 2theta exclusion contours; Radiative decay rate Gamma and X-ray line energy E=m_s/2; X-ray line flux vs NuSTAR M31 and Galactic bulge upper limits.
