**Plan** — 4 lines of investigation:
1. Deepen weak claim (i): BBN alone excludes eV-keV mixing above sin^2 2theta ~1e-4 independent of lepton asymmetry L. Test L-dependence with contrasting emulator calls. — Prior d-01/d-07 showed BBN excludes only large mixing along DW line and leaves DW DM line open, but used DW-only Delta N_eff and heuristic SF (0.1x DW) capped at L<=0.1. Brief and d-03/d-06 note recent BBN analyses allow L>1 at T>20 MeV, weakening exclusions. Need direct contrast: same (m_s, sin^2 2theta) grid evaluated with DW vs SF (large L) vs analytic xi_e shift to show BBN bound moves by 0.1-0.2 in Delta N_eff and |xi_e|<0.03-0.06 reopens parameter space.
2. Deepen weak claim (ii): X-ray non-detections exclude all DW-motivated DM without accounting for alternative production and FOV systematics. Contrast DW vs SF vs inflaton-decay relic density and X-ray flux vs NuSTAR M31/Galactic limits. — Prior d-02/d-08 showed DW line at 7-20 keV is X-ray excluded by built-in limits but at 40-50 keV not excluded yet overcloses, and at 1e-12 requires external limits. Need to show alternative production (SF resonant with L~0.1-1, inflaton-decay BR~1e-4) reopens small-mixing parameter space below X-ray limits, and that M31 1.2 Ms focused+unfocused FOV vs Galactic bulge systematics matter. Requires X-ray line tool + relic density contrast.
3. Literature robustness check: verify 2024-2026 structure-formation (Lyman-alpha, satellite counts, lensing) bounds on m_th and their translation to m_s for each production mechanism. — Prior d-03/d-05/d-06 used m_th>8.4 keV (galaxy counts), >8.5 keV (counts+lensing), and Lyman-alpha m_th=4.1 keV with Viel+2005 mapping m_s=4.43 keV (m_th/keV)^{4/3} but without verbatim quote and with DW-only mapping. Need to check mechanism-dependent free-streaming: DW vs SF vs inflaton-decay produce different momentum distributions, so same m_s corresponds to different m_th. This determines whether reopened small-mixing regions survive structure formation.
4. Board verification and joint BBN+X-ray exclusion overlay with provenance — list_agent_files empty so prior weakest claims unverified; brief requires reproducible joint overlay combining BBN N_eff/Yp/D/H and X-ray flux limits in m_s-sin^2 2theta plane with per-limit provenance and L/BR caveats (added by the critic)
Critic's view: revise — Server caps L<=0.1 (describe_sterile_nu_tools). Heuristic Delta N_eff=0.1x DW for SF is not physical resonant production. Cannot emulator-test L>1 claim from arXiv:2411.07040; must label SF grid as capped illustration and rely on verbatim literature quote for L>0.5-1 BBN consistency, not emulator proof.; list_agent_files=[] and list_input_files=[] so prior d-01/d-07 DW-line results unverified. Must list_files/read_text_file board, SCOPE.md, ISSUES.md before referencing prior exclusions.; Tool budget risk: DW grid + SF L=0.01 + SF L=0.1 =3 predict_sterile_nu_grid calls plus scan_sterile_nu_parameters, plot_sterile_nu_bbn_impact, web_search, read_arxiv_chunk, cite, get_paper_figures approaches 15-call limit. Consolidate to DW + one SF (L=0.1) and drop scan/plot redundancy..
