[finding] f-125 Viel+2005 DW mapping m_s=4.43 keV*(m_th/keV)^{4/3} is DW-specific; SF resonant and inflaton-decay production have colder momentum distributions (<p>/T lower by 
**Finding:** Viel+2005 DW mapping m_s=4.43 keV*(m_th/keV)^{4/3} is DW-specific; SF resonant and inflaton-decay production have colder momentum distributions (<p>/T lower by ~1.5-3x), so same m_s corresponds to larger effective m_th; thus DW m_s>53.7 keV for m_th>6.5 keV (satellites) and >29-49 keV for Lyman-alpha m_th 4.1-6.1 keV does not directly apply to SF/inflaton-decay, which can satisfy structure formation at m_s~10-20 keV with small mixing sin^2 2theta<1e-12 where X-ray limits also weaken.
